1a1/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "0.\n\nNo files were edited. The subagent's first run of `python3 main.py` may have created or updated Python's cache files in `app/__pycache__/`.\n\nWant me to make the fix?\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nI've confirmed it: no other file imports `app.config` or opens `settings.json`. Now the fix:\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI fixed it by renaming the misspelled key in `settings.json` from `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`. All three places that read the setting now work.\n\n**Every place that reads `fee_rate`** (all go through `app/config.py`, which loads `settings.json`):\n\n| File:line | How it reads it | Before the fix | After the fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`, quietly using 0 if missing (lines 10-13) | `Total: 0` | `Total: 5.0` |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` (defined in `app/config.py:13-15`) | stopped with `fee_rate is missing` | `Report fee: 0.5` |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")`, with the name split in two so a plain search for `fee_rate` misses it | stopped with `fee_rate is missing` | `CSV fee: 0.5` |\n\nI checked this with my own searches rather than relying on the subagent. Only `main.py`, `billing/report.py` and `billing/export/csv_writer.py` import `app.config`, and no other file opens `settings.json`. The other files under `billing/` import nothing.\n\nSome files contain look-alike names but don't read the setting:\n- `billing/invoice.py:5` uses the text `\"fee_rate\"` as a column label.\n- `billing/discount.py:5` has its own `archived_fee_rate = 0.15`.\n- `billing/tax.py:5` has its own `fee_schedule`.\n- `billing/audit.py:4` builds a code starting with `\"fee_\"`.\n\nThe before and after results come from running each path with `python3 -B`, so no cache files were written. I didn't change the quiet fallback to 0 in `main.py:10-13`, so a missing key there would still print a total of 0 without any error. I can make it stop with an error like the other two scripts if you'd like.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 180344, "requests_cache_write": 27979, "requests_cost_usd": 0.27678780000000003, "requests_count": 16, "requests_input_uncached": 1596, "requests_output": 4722, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial4", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 13, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T04:27:18.800771+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 3, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 57.649, "t_checker_s": 0.223, "t_env_setup_s": 0.003, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 6318, "tokens_cache_read": 180344, "tokens_cache_write": 27979, "tokens_fresh": 3041, "tokens_input_uncached": 1596, "tokens_main_cache_read": 149764, "tokens_main_cache_write": 10977, "tokens_main_calls": 9, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 22, "tokens_main_output": 3019, "tokens_output": 4722, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 180344, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 27979, "tokens_proxy_calls": 16, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1596, "tokens_proxy_output": 4722, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain":